  "_comment": "Verifier-model catalog for pantheon-custom / pantheon-gap-custom / pantheon-fix-custom, modeled on OpenClaw (docs.openclaw.ai/concepts/model-providers). THIS FILE IS THE SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for provider routing: /pantheon-model reads it for the picker menu, and `node scripts/inline.js` GENERATES the runtime PROVIDERS/ALIASES tables inside every workflow class file from it. Never hand-edit those generated blocks — edit here and re-run the inliner (CI enforces this with `inline.js --check`). Each cloud entry: baseUrl (the OpenAI-compatible root; the drivers POST to `${baseUrl}/chat/completions`) + envKey (the NAME of the API-key env var, NO secret) + wire (chat=OpenAI-compatible, responses=OpenAI Responses, anthropic=Anthropic Messages) + defModel (used when the user names a provider with no model) + models (menu hints). `special` entries (claude/codex/local) are handled natively and are NOT emitted into the runtime table. Pick a model as OpenClaw-style `provider/model-id`.",
  "format": "provider/model-id",
  "_codexComment": "The model the `-x` skills pin for cross-model adversarial verification. The Codex plugin's rescue agent leaves the model UNSET by default, which silently falls back to whatever is in ~/.codex/config.toml — so an `-x` run could be verified by any model while the report still claimed GPT-5.x. The skills now pass this explicitly and record the resolved id in their output. Requires codex-cli >= 0.140 (older builds reject gpt-5.6-* with a 400).",
  "codex": { "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "label": "GPT-5.6 Sol (Codex)", "minCliVersion": "0.140.0" },
